1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:08,848
This sentence is on a product page. In the EU, it is now banned — unless the seller can prove the claim.

2
00:00:10,348 --> 00:00:16,278
Claim Check marks the claims that are now illegal, on the page you are shopping on.

3
00:00:17,378 --> 00:00:29,476
Directive 2024/825 applies from 27 September 2026. It covers stock already on the shelves.

4
00:00:30,776 --> 00:00:40,625
Eco-friendly. Climate neutral. Biodegradable. Without proof, the words are the problem.

5
00:00:41,975 --> 00:00:50,894
It reads the visible text of the page: four banned claims here, two that need evidence.

6
00:00:52,194 --> 00:01:00,744
Each finding quotes the sentence, marks the phrase, and names the article.

7
00:01:02,044 --> 00:01:06,892
Six rules. Four banned practices, and two that need evidence.

8
00:01:09,192 --> 00:01:15,326
It stays quiet when the words are ordinary. Green tea is not a green claim.

9
00:01:17,076 --> 00:01:21,833
One bookmark, any product page. No account, no extension.

10
00:01:23,333 --> 00:01:29,759
The page text never leaves the browser. That is what makes it safe on a checkout page.

11
00:01:31,159 --> 00:01:38,663
Thirteen saved pages. Three findings, all reviewed. A pilot, not a survey.

12
00:01:40,063 --> 00:01:45,957
It cannot see images, it does not judge the product, and it reads English only.

13
00:01:47,557 --> 00:01:52,745
The directive already names the words. Claim Check shows you where they are.
